  "notes": "Cash basis, governmental funds only. Beginning/ending cash are the Cash Basis Fund Balances the statement rolls forward (p4), all cash and cash equivalents (p3). Proceeds from Sale of Bonds 590,550 (Road Fund) printed under other financing sources on the fund statement (p4) -> debt_proceeds; the Statement of Activities (p2) lists it among general receipts. Balance sheet from the governmental funds statement of cash basis assets and fund balances (p3), totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1). Statement Taxes split by fund name (Inheritance Fund); General Fund taxes unlabeled. Detail: General Fund and major funds from the budgetary comparison schedules (pp5-7; ARPA one-line disbursements split by the statement's function columns); 9 nonmajor funds from the combining statement Total column (pp10-11), more detailed than the one-line nonmajor budget schedules (pp8-9), which are not recorded to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-11 of 11 Balances are the printed \"Cash basis fund balances - beginning / ending\" rows, recorded as fund balance like this county's other years (2026-11-19)."
